h2:measurement-characteristics-center-and-spread Measurement characteristics: center and spread
h3:mean-median-and-mode Mean, median, and mode
fig:meanongdp Histogram of country-level GDP per capita (constant 2010 USD) for 2010. The dashed vertical line marks the mean (14,947 USD), while the solid vertical line marks the median (5,206 USD). The large gap between the mean and median reflects the right-skewed distribution of GDP per capita, where a small number of wealthy countries pull the mean far above the median.
